<article class="env-lemma" id="02X2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02X2">Lemma <span data-tag="02X2">65.7.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $F \to H$, $G \to H$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $F \times _ H G$ is an algebraic space, and is a fibre product in the category of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It follows from the stronger Lemma <a href="/tag/04T9" data-tag="04T9">65.7.2</a> that $F \times _ H G$ is an algebraic space. It is clear that $F \times _ H G$ is a fibre product in the category of algebraic spaces over $S$ since that is a full subcategory of the category of (pre)sheaves of sets on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>